{
"dur": 47.656,
"shots": [
{
"i": 1,
"start": 0.0,
"vo_start": 0.6,
"vo_end": 10.52,
"text": "At the WM Phoenix Open, golf's rowdiest week, Jack offered a fan a hundred dollars to shout an insult in the middle of a player's backswing. The fan did it. Jack paid up.",
"end": 10.795
},
{
"i": 2,
"start": 10.795,
"vo_start": 11.07,
"vo_end": 23.908,
"text": "Security and police walked him out. An official told him, on camera, that he was trespassed from every future PGA Tour event. Jack asked: forever? For the foreseeable future, came the answer.",
"end": 24.183
},
{
"i": 3,
"start": 24.183,
"vo_start": 24.458,
"vo_end": 32.292,
"text": "Jack called it the most harmless prank he could have done. The golfer, Mackenzie Hughes, still made the cut, and said he didn't lose much sleep over it.",
"end": 32.567
},
{
"i": 4,
"start": 32.567,
"vo_start": 32.842,
"vo_end": 46.706,
"text": "But look at the bill. A supermarket stunt costs you a supermarket. This one cost him an entire sport. Same pattern as twenty seventeen. The difference is that the places kicking him out had started keeping a list.",
"end": 47.656
}
],
